    - target: {fileID: 5545414368755638688, guid: 11889ddad84efa74cb6476a97ba23853, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_Name
      value: StoryUICanvas
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 7601046077032374988, guid: 11889ddad84efa74cb6476a97ba23853, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: "The Sun and The Moon\n\nLong ago, the Earth was created and ruled by
        Bathala.  \n\nHe had two children\u2014Apolaqui and Mayari. From the eyes
        of these two children, the Earth got its first light. \n\nThe people, birds,
        animals, and even the fishes rejoiced, for the world was no longer in darkness.
        They became great friends with Apolaqui and Mayari.\n\nBathala loved his
        children dearly and never wanted to be apart from them. So, no matter how
        tired he was, he always followed them on their daily walks. \n\nBut as time
        passed, Bathala grew old and weak. Eventually, he could no longer keep up.\n\nHe
        asked them to stay with him, but the children, too caught up in their fun,
        ignored their father\u2019s wish.\n \nOne day, Bathala grew gravely ill and
        died without leaving any instructions about who should rule the Earth. \n\nApolaqui
        wanted to take the throne for himself and rule alone. But Mayari refused\u2014she
        believed they should share responsibilities as equals.\n\nA fierce argument
        between Apolaqui and Mayari quickly became an all-out battle beneath the
        darkening skies.\n\nThe wind howled through the trees as the two celestial
        siblings faced each other, bamboo clubs in hand\u2014eyes burning not with
        light, but with anger and heartbreak.\n\n\nApolaqui took a fierce stance,
        his grip tightening around his weapon. His aura radiating with the blinding
        strength of the sun. \n\nWhile Mayari, confident and graceful, stood firm
        like a calm before the storm, her moonlit presence casting a silver glow
        around her.\n\nThe clash was swift and brutal.\n\nWood met wood in thunderous
        echoes. Sparks flew from each strike as their powers collided\u2014sunlight
        against moonbeams.\n\nMayari moved with elegance and precision, her attacks
        moving like waves of the tides. \n\nApolaqui countered with brute force and
        relentless energy, each swing growing heavier and heavier.\n\nThey fought
        for what felt like an eternity, a dance of light and shadows.\n\nBut eventually,
        Apolaqui gained the upper hand.\n\nWith one final blow, his club struck true\u2014landing
        across Mayari\u2019s face. She cried out in pain as light burst from her
        wounded eye like a dying star.\n\nShe collapsed on her knees, hands covering
        her face, her once radiant glow flickering like a candle in the wind.\n\nSilence
        fell.\n\nApolaqui stared at her, wide-eyed. The club slipped from his hand
        and hit the ground with a dull thud.\n\n\u201CWhat have I done\u2026?\u201D
        he whispered, voice trembling. \u201CHow foolish was I\u2026 to let greed
        blind me. Our father\u2014he would never have wanted this.\u201D\n\nThrough
        the pain, Mayari looked up at him, her face soft with forgiveness. Despite
        her injury, she managed a small smile.\n\n\u201CBrother\u2026 It\u2019s not
        too late.\u201D\n\nTears appeared in Apolaqui\u2019s eyes. He knelt beside
        her, taking her hand in his. At that moment, the flames of his pride were
        extinguished.\n\nIn their place, a new light was born\u2014one of humility
        and of love.\n\nMayari\u2019s brilliance had dimmed\u2014her remaining eye
        casting only a gentle, silver glow\u2014but Apolaqui refused to let her fade
        into darkness. He vowed to make things right.\n\nThat very night, he rose
        before the heavens and declared, \u201CWe shall fight no more. From now on,
        we share this world.\n\nI shall shine during the day\u2026 and Mayari shall
        reign in the night.\u201D\n\nAnd so, the balance was restored.\n\nApolaqui,
        now called the Sun, blazed across the sky by day, casting his golden light
        over the Earth.\n\nMayari, the Moon, graces the night with her soft, gentle
        glow\u2014a quiet reminder of sacrifice, and of the bond that even pride
        could not sever.\n\nTo this day, their light continues to guide us\u2014two
        siblings, forever taking turns in the sky.\n\n\u2013 THE END \u2013\n"
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
